b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ HARNESS POSING incremental;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE author: implementation-algol-60, an agent (Claude Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE precursor seen: no;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE idioms: the Revised Report on ALGOL 60 (1962) for blocks, procedures (5.4), the for statement with a while element (4.6), conditional statements and expressions (3.3, 4.5) and the Boolean operator of negation (3.4), the X1 system's input and output procedures read, print, PRINTTEXT and NLCR, as the harness README gives them (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.1) and its own X1 programs cite them (Kruseman Aretz 2003, chapter 7), and the X1 compiler's representation, with underlined reserved words and the operator symbols (harness README, 2.1), the message loop and observe block of the harness README example X01 (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.8), and the holding of each relation until its unknown is known, written for this problem (METRICS.md, rule 19), with no period source;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ CONSTANTS a line 1: c, the integer of x = c. A line 2: d, the integer of not (x = d);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ P06b. One unknown x. Stage 1: x = c1. Stage 2: not (x = c2). x is a Boolean that says whether it has a value and an integer that holds it. Each relation is held as posed until x is known: then the equation gives x its value, or is tested, and the negation is tested. The negation of an equation whose unknown has no value is not decided: it is held;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ n, cap, m, i, code, k, c1, c2, xv, held, pass, x1, x2;
  b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ xk, r1, r2, changed, inconsistent;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ examine1;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the evaluator of x = c1: with x known, it is tested, else x is given the value c1;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    x1 := x1 + 1;
    i̲f̲ xk t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ i̲f̲ ¬(xv = c1) t̲h̲e̲n̲ inconsistent := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ xv := c1; xk := t̲r̲u̲e̲; changed := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲;
    r1 := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲
  e̲n̲d̲ examine1;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ examine2;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the evaluator of not (x = c2): with x known, it is tested. With x unknown, it waits;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    x2 := x2 + 1;
    i̲f̲ xk t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ i̲f̲ ¬(xv = c2) t̲h̲e̲n̲ r2 := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲ e̲l̲s̲e̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ inconsistent := t̲r̲u̲e̲; r2 := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲ e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ examine2;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ propagate;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ every held relation is examined, in the order posed, again and again until a whole pass gives x no value;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    changed := t̲r̲u̲e̲;
    f̲o̲r̲ pass := 1 w̲h̲i̲l̲e̲ changed d̲o̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      changed := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲;
      i̲f̲ r1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ examine1;
      i̲f̲ r2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ examine2
    e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ propagate;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ relations;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: the relations held, with the value of x put in its place if known;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲f̲ r1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`x = '); print(c1) e̲n̲d̲;
    i̲f̲ r2 t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      i̲f̲ r1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`, ');
      PRINTTEXT(`not (x = '); print(c2); PRINTTEXT(`)')
    e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ relations;

  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ harness words: the instance line;
  n := read; cap := read; m := read;
  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ m d̲o̲ code := read;
  xk := r1 := r2 := inconsistent := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲;
  x1 := x2 := 0;

  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 w̲h̲i̲l̲e̲ t̲r̲u̲e̲ d̲o̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ harness words: one message, the stage it poses, and then that stage's constants;
    code := read; k := read;
    i̲f̲ k = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ c1 := read; r1 := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ k = 2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ c2 := read; r2 := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲;

    propagate;

    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the answer: x, and the relations still held;
    i̲f̲ ¬inconsistent t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      PRINTTEXT(`[answer]x');
      i̲f̲ xk t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(` = '); print(xv) e̲n̲d̲
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ r1 ∨ r2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(` held') e̲l̲s̲e̲ PRINTTEXT(` free');
      i̲f̲ r1 ∨ r2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`, where '); relations e̲n̲d̲;
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/answer]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲
    e̲n̲d̲;

    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ observe: the relations held, the value known, how many relations wait, and how often each was examined;
    held := (i̲f̲ r1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ 1 e̲l̲s̲e̲ 0) + (i̲f̲ r2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ 1 e̲l̲s̲e̲ 0);
    PRINTTEXT(`[observe]');
    i̲f̲ inconsistent t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`no solution'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`held relations: ');
    i̲f̲ held = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`none') e̲l̲s̲e̲ relations;
    NLCR;
    i̲f̲ xk t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[bind x]'); print(xv); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/bind]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲ e̲n̲d̲;
    i̲f̲ held > 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[suspended held-relations '); print(held); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲ e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`[operations eq-examined '); print(x1); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`[operations not-eq-examined '); print(x2); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/observe]'); NLCR; PRINTTEXT(`[end]') e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲
e̲n̲d̲
